  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The equation of the curve whose slope at any point is equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></math> and which passes through the origin is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "DZYl8",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Z4k45",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "dJjic",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Gzaz9",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>IF</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi></math> be the constant of integration</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8747;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp; [using integration by parts]</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>As curve (i) passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Thus, the curve is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence, option (b) is correct.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
